[00:31:53] ## Worth your attention
[00:31:53] I recorded a real gap as `KNOWN_PROBLEMS.md` §7.12 rather than designing around it: since an item absent from `tp_tradeable_items` is classified non-Trading-Post, a never-synchronized or half-rewritten table classifies *everything* as non-Trading-Post. With the option off that would block nearly every path with truthful-but-misleading reasons, and nothing tells the user the classification itself is stale. The enabled default is unaffected (no query is issued). Also note `ResolutionState.UNVALUED_NONTRADEABLE` still derives from a `<= 0` sell unit under §11.2 — untouched here, but it shares the word "nontradeable" with the new classification while meaning something different.
